            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0016" n="4" xml:id="pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation (2)A/50</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Adviser on Political Relations</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Duggan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-14">April 14, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Welles</hi>: The Inter-American Commission for
                    Territorial Administration may now be convened at any moment by any country
                    adhering to the Habana Convention, as a result of the approval voted by the
                    Governing Board of the Pan American Union at its last meeting of a resolution
                    interpreting the Convention to provide that the Emergency Committee (Act of
                    Habana) automatically becomes the Commission for Territorial Administration
                    (Convention of Habana).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurence Duggan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
